Weather icons
=============

The SVG files in this directory are derived from Meteocons by Bas Milius, used under the MIT License.

Each file's root viewBox is rewritten so that motifs shared between icons render at a consistent size, with stroke widths rescaled to keep line weight even.

Position is not normalized. Each viewBox is centered on its artwork. (The cloud sits higher in the icons that need room for precipitation below it.)

An icon may take another icon's stroke attributes. (In `partly-cloudy-night.svg` the moon takes the rounded line join and line cap of the full-size crescent in `clear-night.svg`.)

The path data, colors, and animations are unchanged.

Source: https://github.com/basmilius/meteocons

